{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightAnnihilation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightAnnihilation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightTelescope"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.instStrongAJFigureEightOfCharZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.instStrongAJFigureEightOfCharZero","kind":"instance","line":483,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L483-L495","doc":"**Strong AJ for the figure-eight — every field is machine-checked.**\nSupersedes the cited-sorry instance formerly in `AJFigureEight.lean`:\nthe general-`N` annihilation is the proved\n`figureEightOperator_annihilates` (division-free certificate\ntelescope, valid at every `q ≠ 0` including roots of unity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_annihilates","kind":"theorem","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L391-L477","doc":"**General-`N` annihilation, proved for every `q ≠ 0`** (roots of unity\nincluded): the explicit operator annihilates the colored Jones tower\nof the figure-eight.  `N = 0` is a direct computation; `N ≥ 1` is the\ndivision-free certificate telescope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_local_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_local_step","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L191-L382","doc":"**Local step at `k = m + 2` — the master identity.**  All divisions are\nby powers of `q`, `x` and by `clearD` (nonzero); the B-side shift\ndenominators `(xq−1)`, `(xq²−1)` are consumed exactly by the factors\nthe operator supplies, so the identity holds for every `q ≠ 0` —\nroots of unity included ([K3] + [SIM] in the pre-verification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_local_step_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_local_step_one","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L141-L189","doc":"Local step at `k = 1`: the three ladder factors are the explicit\n`Λ_M − λ₁`, and `certW 2` is the explicit cleared form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_local_step_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_local_step_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L128-L139","doc":"Local step at `k = 0` (all three ladder values are `1`):\n`a₂ + a₁ + a₀ = certW(1) − certW(0)` — the boundary identity\n`W(0) = −rhs` in step form ([W0] in the pre-verification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_top_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW_top_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L104-L120","doc":"**Top of the tower**: at `x = q^N` with `N ≥ 1` the telescoping\nsequence vanishes at `k = N + 2` — the `j = N − 1` factor of\n`risingA q (q^N) N` is `q^N − q^N = 0`.  Division-free, so no\ngenericity hypothesis is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.certW","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L85-L102","doc":"The certificate telescoping sequence, division-free.  `certW q x k` is\nthe pole-cleared value of `Cert(q, x, q^k) · F(N, k)`:\n\n* `k = 0`: `−rhs(q,x)` (the boundary value `−Cert(x,1)` — the content\n  of `feCert_boundary`);\n* `k = 1`: the explicit cleared value;\n* `k ≥ 2`: `−C·(1−x)(1−qx)·q^k·A(k−2)·B(k) / (q²x⁷·clearD(k))` with\n  `C = (qx+1)(qx²−1)(q³x²−1)` — divisions only by powers and `clearD`,\n  all nonzero for `q, x ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD_shift","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L73-L81","doc":"Color shift of the clearing product: `clearD_{qx}(k) = q^k · clearD_x(k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L69-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD_succ","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L65-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.clearD","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightAnnihilation.lean#L60-L63","doc":"`clearD q x k = ∏_{j<k} x·q^{j+1}` — the per-factor denominators of the\nNewton ladder at `x + x⁻¹`, as one product (nonzero for `q, x ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}